{
  "work_package_id": "WP-008",
  "work_package_file": "work/WP-008.md",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "assigned_to": "QA",
  "dependencies": [
    "WP-005"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "The credentials table in settings renders columns: Label, Host, Token, Actions.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The add credential form includes a required \"Label\" field, with Host and Token fields, and button text \"Add Credential\".",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Clicking \"Edit\" on a credential row enables inline editing of Label and Token fields; Host is read-only.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Clicking \"Save\" after inline editing calls PUT /api/config/credentials with the existing credential id and updated fields.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Delete button calls DELETE /api/config/credentials/:id (by credential id, not host).",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "When deleting a credential referenced by repositories, the confirmation dialog warns: \"Remove credential '{label}'? {N} repository/repositories currently use this credential and will lose their credential association.\"",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "When deleting a credential not referenced by any repository, the confirmation dialog shows: \"Remove credential '{label}' for host '{host}'? This action cannot be undone.\"",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "api.config.credentials.add() sends PUT /api/config/credentials with the correct body (no id).",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "api.config.credentials.update(id, data) sends PUT /api/config/credentials with the existing id in the body.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "api.config.credentials.remove(id) sends DELETE /api/config/credentials/:id.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "All GUI tests in settings.test.mjs and api.config.test.mjs pass.",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T13:12:12Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T13:21:52Z",
      "duration_ms": 580000,
      "summary": [
        "Updated api.js credentials namespace: renamed set()→add(), added update(id, data) sending PUT with id in body, renamed delete(host)→remove(id) sending DELETE /api/config/credentials/:id.",
        "Updated settings.js buildTableHead() to emit Label, Host, Token, Actions columns. Rewrote buildCredentialRow() to accept a credential object {id, label, host, maskedToken}, add Label cell with inline edit input, Token cell with password input for edit mode, host cell always read-only, Edit/Save/Cancel action buttons, and delete flow that fetches repositories to check for references and builds the correct confirmation message.",
        "Updated buildAddCredentialForm() to include a required Label field before Host, changed submit button text to 'Add Credential', calls api.config.credentials.add().",
        "Updated renderCredentialsTable() to iterate over an array (not Object.entries) of credential objects.",
        "Updated settings.test.mjs: corrected AC3 tests for new data shape (array vs object), added AC-T1 through AC-T7 tests covering new column headers, add form label field, inline edit mode, save calls update with id, remove called with id not host, and delete confirmation message variants.",
        "Updated api.config.test.mjs: added structure, list, add, update, and remove tests verifying correct HTTP method, URL, and body shape for all new credential API client methods.",
        "All 17 settings.test.mjs and 23 api.config.test.mjs tests pass. Other test suites unaffected."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "gui/public/js/api.js",
          "gui/public/js/views/settings.js",
          "gui/public/js/views/settings.test.mjs",
          "gui/public/js/api.config.test.mjs"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:21:52Z",
          "note": "settings.js buildCredentialRow(): the cred object passed to the row builder is the same reference returned from api.config.credentials.list(). Mutating cred.label on save works but creates an implicit coupling between the list cache and the row state. Consider returning a new credential object from the update call and re-rendering the row, or using a local state variable for the current label to avoid this coupling. Not a bug — noted as a design observation."
        },
        {
          "type": "refactor",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:21:52Z",
          "note": "settings.js: the enter/escape keydown handler is only attached to labelInput, not to tokenInput. Adding an equivalent handler on tokenInput would improve keyboard UX (consistent with the repositories inline-edit pattern which attaches the handler to its single input). Out of WP-008 scope but worth noting."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:21:52Z",
          "note": "api.config.test.mjs: the test file previously had no tests for api.config.credentials — the old set()/delete(host) methods were untested. This debt is now addressed by the new add/update/remove tests added in WP-008."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:21:52Z",
          "note": "settings.test.mjs: showConfirm (ESM export from confirm-dialog.js) cannot be easily monkey-patched in the Node test environment without dynamic import tricks. The AC-T6/AC-T7 tests verify the message-building logic indirectly by checking the repositories mock and expected message format rather than intercepting the confirm dialog call. This is consistent with the existing test approach in the file and is acceptable, but worth noting for future test infrastructure improvements."
        }
      ]
    },
